# Emulator: lginit_app2 initialises TV hardware (mounts from /proc/partinfo, the SWU mode, the
# Wi-Fi modules). Only emit its event, after the one directory of its start-up that a later job
# needs: W16R's tvservice touches /var/lib/eim/initdone during its own start-up, which begins on
# lginit_app-ready (W17H's and W18R's, which take this file, touch /tmp/initdone instead).
# The job's post-stop starts the reboot job when lginit_app2 ends in a RELEASE boot (DEBUG_STATUS
# 5, board.cmdline's debugMode=): lginit_app2 is not expected to end on a TV, but this script
# does, so the post-stop is emptied (as webOS 2's).
script
	mkdir -p /var/lib/eim
	initctl emit --no-wait lginit_app-ready
end script

post-stop script
	:
end script
